    {
      "id": 136836,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-10T13:36:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"cmschex\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/e9bcb4/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> cmschex:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Unless that cowboy travels through time i dont really see that being an issue…even then, comic tropes are not IP enforceable. &nbsp;I mean, much of the SotM lineup have clear homages to existing characters.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>But we are talking about a cowboy bounty hunter with the same hat, cigar problem, shoulder poncho, favors a pistol, uses grenades, and has a robotic left arm.</p>\n<p>There is a big difference between playing with comic tropes and flat out copying characters. I'm not saying that Blizzard is stealing Chrono Ranger here, but there is a lot more than just a passing resemblance there. Certainly calls it into question.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also, Tracer is Tachyon, Hanzo is like Parse, and Widowmaker is like The Wraith.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>These are not even remotely close to the same ballpark as the Chrono similarities.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:13:06.118Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
